# One item per assertion, question, withdrawal, or proposed check.
add('N01','002, cover diagrams','unproved claim / reading question','modéré; β injectif',f'{C147}, scans 150,155 (gluing systems); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.1–C.6','adds a diagrammatic presentation problem; identification of its faint map labels remains insecure','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; STRATA C.1–C.6 [return claims]',r'The cover puts coequalizer-like coproduct arrows, fibre products and a monomorphism β beside conditions on composites β∘p_i, without an accompanying proof. The actual objects and arrow directions must be used to formulate the desired presentation before comparing it with the crossing-category construction in the context; the repeated absolute-value bars in the lower diagrams cannot themselves establish a realization theorem. No result about all spaces over a base follows from these cover calculations.', ['recollement','coprod','morphismes'])
add('N02','004, characteristic functions','unpursued implication',"la donnée de F équivaut à celle de la partie",f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (partitions and local stratification); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, BISITE D.2','adds an algebraic encoding of admissible subsets before the later stratification apparatus','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.2 [return claim]',r'The displayed correspondence has explicit maps: A is sent to its characteristic function φ_A, and F is recovered as the subsets A for which φ_A belongs to the specified algebra. The elementary identities φ_{A∩B}=φ_Aφ_B and φ_{X\A}=1−φ_A explain the Boolean operations that this encoding records. Passing from this algebra of functions to a sheaf or a category of geometric coefficients still requires the additional constructions on020–024 and039.', ['partition','faisceau','fonctions'])
add('N03','005, opening paragraph','unproved claim',r'on peut \unsure{prouver|penser}',f'{C147}, scans 181–182; no corresponding fraction-field assertion found in either supplied context transcription','adds a separate algebraic assertion; no matching proof located','No directly settling RESULTS_STATE entry; WG2 B15 (§1.2) is only thematic [unchecked plan]',r'The manuscript characterizes the algebras arising from F by a saturation property inside finite-valued functions over an integral coefficient ring and its fraction field. It does not prove this paragraph: the missing work is recovery of every characteristic idempotent from the finite values of a function and descent back to the original coefficient ring. The uncertain verb stays uncertain; this note records the stated characterization without treating it as a completed result.', ['fonctions','anneau','algèbre'])
add('N04','005 and010; intermediate009 margin','withdrawn in the same text','les composantes connexes; Condition f)',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,184','adds the earlier revision of the finiteness/local-connectedness conditions later used for strata','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The cancelled d) on005 includes local connectedness, whereas010 installs a live f) requiring finitely many connected components belonging to F. The cancelled009 margin places those components in F_0;010 writes F. These are revisions of the stated axioms, and their locations should accompany any quotation of the tame-space conditions.', ['connexes','loc. connexes','stratification'])
add('N05','006, Boolean-generation NB','reading question / own explicit check','avec A,B∈Φ',f'{C147}, scans 181–182; no matching Boolean-generation lemma found','adds a finite check of a literal algebraic formula','No directly settling RESULTS_STATE entry; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'For the literal formula on the page take X={1,2} and Φ={{1}}: every displayed A∩complement(B), with A,B∈Φ, is empty, so their finite unions produce only the empty set, whereas the Boolean algebra generated by Φ contains {1},{2},X. This computation identifies a missing closure or extra terms in that literal formula; it does not authorize changing Φ in the transcription. This is our check, with high confidence because all four subsets are explicitly enumerated, and no novelty claim.', ['parties','réunion','complémentaire'])
add('N06','006 and009, boundary induction','unproved claim (with a manuscript proof sketch)','F est “engendré” pr l’ens des parties fermées',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (closure and local models)','adds a termination argument for the admissible Boolean family, preceding the later local stratification framework','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The proposed induction replaces X by the boundary of A and terminates by e);009 returns to the needed rarity of the boundary and uses restriction to its interior. A proof audit should track the restricted family F|X_n and the density statement at each stage, since those are the actual transitions written in the proof. The later localization discussion on019 supplies related inheritance arguments, so this is a dispersed argument rather than an isolated declaration.', ['adhérence','local','fermé'])
add('N07','007, opening question','self-flagged / question','Est-ce suffisant',f'{C147}, scan181 (closure axioms); no corresponding answer for closed-family Boolean generation found','adds a question about recovering the closed members of F','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'He asks whether closure of F_0 under finite unions and intersections already makes it exactly the closed part of its generated Boolean family. The page then introduces γ, closure of A∩complement(B), as an additional condition and develops its consequences; this does not by itself answer the earlier question under α and β alone. The question remains separately recorded even though its strengthened replacement is pursued immediately.', ['fermés','réunions','intersections'])
add('N08','007, same question','own idea — explicit finite check','Est-ce suffisant',f'{C147}, scan181; related search as N07','adds a fully enumerated counterexample to the α/β-only reading','No directly settling RESULTS_STATE entry; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'On discrete X={1,2,3}, the family F_0={∅,{2},{1,2},{2,3},X} is closed under finite intersections and unions. The Boolean difference {1,2}\{2,3}={1} is closed in X and belongs to the generated Boolean family, but is absent from F_0. This answers the α/β-only question in this concrete form; confidence is high because the displayed five-member family is closed under both operations and the missing singleton is explicit.', ['fermés','réunions','intersections'])
add('N09','007–009, γ/δ and topology reconstruction','unproved claim (with proof sketch)','quand il existe une top. sur X',f'{C147}, scans182–183 (local data and their realization)','adds an explicit coarsest-topology construction, at a different level of input data','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The answer on009 builds closed sets as arbitrary intersections of members of F_0 and gives the additional minimum-closed-superset condition γ′. The maps being used are literal closure operations A↦intersection{C∈F_0:A⊆C}, not the open-test localization functor C_Y in the context register. Thus the page adds a concrete topological construction to the broader realization discussion while leaving BISITE D.12’s category-level comparison unaddressed.', ['topologie','local','faisceau'])
add('N10','010, final paragraph','unproved claim','en fait cette restriction est inutile',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,184','restates the importance of connected components under open restriction, with a different stated input family','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The manuscript asserts local connectedness from f) and the hypothesis that F-open sets form a topological basis, then removes the locally-closed restriction in a parenthesis. The needed verification passes from arbitrary A∈F to a finite decomposition by locally closed pieces and follows the connected components of their restrictions. The later proof on019–020 addresses finiteness and membership of components, so both passages belong in an audit of that parenthetical strengthening.', ['connexes','ouvert','local'])
add('N11','011–012, revised condition2','withdrawn in the same text / reading question','Mais 1° + les X_i loc. fermés n’implique …',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (conditions a–e)','adds the earlier cancelled argument and its finite-partition replacement','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'On011 the attempted condition and proof involving locally closed pieces are heavily cancelled; the live condition2 is equality of closures implying equality of leaves, and012 gives an induction proving local closedness from1 and2. The marginal example X={x}∪(X\{x}) is explicitly part of the author’s objection, but the antecedent of the cramped word “ceci” remains uncertain. The note records the withdrawal and replacement without assigning that marginal counterexample a stronger target than the ink supports.', ['strates','adhérence','loc. fermés'])
add('N12','012–013, strictness proof','reading question','d)⇒3); 3)⇒d)',f'{C147}, scan181 (connected-stratum condition)','differs in the literal condition letter while the surrounding subject matches connectedness','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The prose announces an equivalence with f), but the two displayed implication labels visibly use d). This discrepancy is preserved in the frozen text; the relevant later context speaks directly about connected strata and supplies no palaeographic evidence for replacing the written letter. A mathematical reading should cite the prose and the literal labels together.', ['connexes','condition','strates'])
add('N13','013–014, finite quotient','unpursued implication','la relation d’incidence est la relation de spécialisation',f'{C147}, scans185–188 (flag spaces and their composition); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, BISITE D.2','adds the explicit quotient map preceding the context’s flag categories','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; BISITE G.10 and BISITE D.2 [return claims]',r'The concrete map is q:X→I, sending a point to its leaf, and the manuscript identifies q^{-1}(closure{i}) with closure(X_i). This gives the stated incidence/specialization dictionary on the finite quotient and links chains in I with the flags later written in147. BISITE D.2 and G.10 already record broader realization comparisons as return claims; these pages add manuscript evidence for the indexing map, not a new proof of those comparisons.', ['drapeau','catégorie','strates'])
add('N14','015–016, existence and least partition','unproved claim (with induction sketch)','une plus … grossière',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,185 (strata and flags)','adds a coarsest admissible-partition construction upstream of the context','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The construction removes the finite union of boundaries, partitions its complement, adds the traces of closures to Φ′, and invokes e) to terminate. Existence and leastness are both asserted, so verification must check minimality under refinement as well as termination. In particular the added closure traces are necessary data for the recursive comparison, and should not be omitted in a later formulation.', ['partition','fermé','strates'])
add('N15','015 and018, Boolean atoms','reading question','une intersection … des tels ensembles Y∩U',f'{C147}, scan181; no formula for these Boolean atoms located','adds a local proof-reading issue;018 explicitly inserts complement stability','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The015 sentence describes each U_i using intersections of Y∩U, while018 explicitly writes the instruction to make Φ stable under complement. For X={1,2} and Φ={{1}}, the atom {2} already requires a complement, so the literal015 wording alone does not list every atom. The018 insertion supplies an internal manuscript lead to the required operation; no word or symbol has been added to015.', ['parties','complémentaire','partition'])
add('N16','016–017, cancelled Dim','withdrawn in the same text','(Dim); satisfait … d) e)',f'{C147}, scans 181,184 (local finiteness and compactness)','adds a revision of the termination hypothesis','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The separate Dim paragraph is cancelled and the corollaries are rewritten to cite e). The finite-dimensional marginal remark is itself weakly read, so it should not be promoted to a uniform numerical dimension theorem. The stronger uniform bound is introduced explicitly only at024 as e_n.', ['fini','dimension','compact'])
add('N17','017, connected refinement','unproved claim (proof referred back)','La dém. est la même',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (refinement by connected components)','restates the connected-component refinement method','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The author replaces the U_i of015 by their connected components to obtain a least strict admissible partition and finite suprema. This refers back to the previous induction rather than repeating its leastness argument, and f) supplies the finiteness needed at the new step. The context’s later passage to components under open restriction is a related operation with its own local-finiteness conditions.', ['composantes connexes','stratification','partition'])
add('N18','017–018, regularity definition','withdrawn in the same text','Ceci implique que les feuilles sont ∈F_r',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (compatibility along closures)','adds a stronger compatibility requirement on regular loci of saturated closed sets','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The original requirement that the leaves belong to F_r is cancelled and replaced by stability of the regularity structure on F_P, expressed through singular loci of saturated closed subsets. The underlined sentence explicitly makes regular leaves a consequence of the replacement. This revision should accompany any comparison with a named stratification notion; leafwise regularity alone omits the extra compatibility actually written here.', ['strates','fermé','local'])
add('N19','018, proposition and three corollaries','unproved claim (recursive outline)','Partition F-régulière canonique de X',f'{C147}, scans 181–182; STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.5','adds canonical regular-partition assertions to the later use of stratifications','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The proof adds singular loci of closures to the recursive family and asserts existence, a least regular partition, finite suprema and a canonical partition. The final corollary has no separate proof, and the hypotheses/compatibility with the displayed finite Φ need to be retained when reconstructing the argument. The regularity condition’s B/S label and the later d)/f) references remain reading issues, not silently repaired assumptions.', ['stratification','drapeau','fermé'])
add('N20','019, localization to A','self-flagged (answered by proof sketch)','satisfait-il aussi d) et e)?',f'{C147}, scans182,184 (restriction to opens)','adds an inheritance argument for admissible subsets','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The paragraph answers its own question using generation by relatively closed sets and closure of a descending chain in X. The margin then extends the trace construction to an arbitrary subset A, an additional assertion that is broader than the opening A∈F case. Neither passage constructs the realization/localization equivalence asked for in BISITE D.12.', ['restriction','ouvert','local'])
add('N21','019 margin','unproved claim','une partie quelconque A de X',f'{C147}, scans182,184','differs in scope: arbitrary-subset traces versus the context’s open restriction','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The margin defines F_A={B∩A:B∈F} for arbitrary A and asserts a–e. A proof must explicitly compute closures in the subspace A and check the rare-chain condition for this trace family, since the body initially identifies F_A with the members of F contained in an admissible A. The literal two definitions therefore need their separate domains when this assertion is used.', ['restriction','local','stratification'])
add('N22','019–020, components of arbitrary admissible A','unproved claim (completed short argument)','les composantes connexes de A sont réunions de Z_i',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (component refinement)','restates the mechanism of passing from pieces to connected components','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The short proof decomposes A into finitely many connected locally closed Z_i, then observes that every component is a union of such pieces. This supplies the finite-component assertion needed earlier on010 and records an internal completion of that part of the argument. The proof’s finite decomposition is essential data, especially beside the later discussion of arbitrary opens.', ['composantes','loc. fermés','connexes'])
add('N23','020, sheafification','self-flagged','Il n’est pas clair qu’il satisfait e)',f'{C147}, scans182–184 (associated sheaf and global leaves)','adds explicit questions about a sheaf of admissible subsets','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The author leaves two assertions open: preservation of e) by F↦overline F and generation of overline F by its closed members. The equality overline(overline F)=overline F is stated separately and does not prove either assertion. The later e_n on024 is a strengthened axiom introduced to manage this difficulty, not a retrospective proof that every original sheafification satisfies e).', ['faisceau','locale','compact'])
add('N24','020–021, compact equality','withdrawn/qualified across the text','si X est quasi-compact … F=overline F',f'{C147}, scans182,184','adds an exact basis-dependence to the local/global comparison','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'On020 the equality uses a finite subcover by F-open sets, under the explicitly stated basis hypothesis. On021 he removes that basis hypothesis and says compactness alone does not justify the equality. These are different stated domains connected by the operation of dropping the basis assumption; the note records that operation rather than calling the two sentences an unexplained contradiction.', ['faisceau','compact','ouverts'])
add('N25','021, compactness warning','own idea — explicit example','même si X compact',f'{C147}, scan182 (associated sheaf)','adds a concrete two-point calculation of the warning','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'Take the compact discrete space X={a,b} and F={∅,X}. Every subset is locally represented by ∅ or X on the singleton opens, so Γ(X,Φ_F)=P(X) has four elements while F has two. This is our high-confidence check of the manuscript’s warning: the local representatives and the inclusion F→Γ(X,Φ_F) are completely explicit.', ['faisceau','localement','compact'])
add('N26','021–022, first saturation question','self-flagged (answered in the next scan)','Cela est-il suffisant',f'{C147}, scan182 (global data known locally)','adds an argument about local unions of connected leaves','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The question on021 concerns equality over the specified admissible open U, and022 argues by the open-and-closed intersection of a locally saturated A with each connected leaf. The literal first paragraph says “de A” at one point; the later paragraph explicitly places the relevant clopen intersections in X_i∩U, so the proof-reading issue must remain visible. The “Non” further down022 addresses a subsequent converse about arbitrary unions of components, not the first question without this intervening change of statement.', ['localement','connexes','faisceau'])
add('N27','022, converse and examples','self-flagged / counterexample','Non',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (germ connectedness and local stratifications)','adds a counterexample controlling which component unions are local sections','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The real-line example separates the two halves of the punctured leaf but shows that the chosen half does not become a section through the distinguished point. The compactified-line example preserves connectedness of the original open leaf while its intersection with the chosen smaller open splits. These examples bear directly on the context’s additional germ-connectedness requirement and must not be condensed into an assertion that all component unions are locally admissible.', ['connexe','germe','stratification'])
add('N28','023, arbitrary-open restriction','unproved claim','n’est pas stable par restriction à un ouvert quelconque',f'{C147}, scans182,184','restates the loss of global finiteness under open restriction','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The page explicitly separates restriction to an F-open set from restriction to an arbitrary topological open, and then asks for local finiteness of connected components. In the context,147/184 likewise says the finite-number-of-strata condition is not stable under passage to an open. The new page gives the family F formulation and a local proof attempt, rather than settling every globalization question in the register.', ['ouvert','fini','composantes'])
add('N29','023, same restriction issue','own idea — explicit example','ouvert quelconque',f'{C147}, scan184','adds a concrete restriction map exhibiting the asserted failure of global finiteness','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'For the semialgebraic family on R, take U=union over integers n of (n,n+1/2) and the inclusion j:U→R. The trace j^{-1}(R)=U has the infinitely many displayed intervals as connected components, although the original member R has one component. This is our high-confidence example because each gap separates consecutive intervals and each interval is connected; it addresses the finite-component clause only, without claiming a classification of all locally tame structures.', ['ouvert','composantes','fini'])
add('N30','023, underlined question','self-flagged','Elle est … locᵗ finie dans U?',f'{C147}, scans182,184','adds an explicit local-finiteness check behind the later open-restriction assertion','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The author distinguishes local finiteness inside A or a smaller V from local finiteness in the ambient open U. After a cancelled start he invokes neighbourhoods on which A is represented by an F-member with finitely many components. The question and its surviving argument should both be retained in a proof audit, including the basis hypothesis in the margin.', ['loc. finie','composantes','ouvert'])
add('N31','023–024, sheaf version of e)','unproved claim / reformulation','la suite des X_i est loc finie sur U',f'{C147}, scans 181,184 (local finiteness versus compact global finiteness)','adds a local termination axiom and its compact-space consequence','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The revised axiom requires a descending chain to disappear locally, and024 derives eventual disappearance on each quasi-compact K. The global e) is then asserted for quasi-compact X, making the compactness step explicit. The uncertain n+2/n+1 subscript in023 is a reading question and cannot be used to silently choose a different axiom.', ['loc. finie','compact','fini'])
add('N32','024, first paragraph','self-flagged','il satisfait à e) si ???',f'{C147}, scans182–184','adds an unresolved restriction problem for the sheaf-defined family','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The three question marks leave the required condition on A unstated. The subsequent uniform e_n is explicitly introduced as a stronger axiom and yields a claim for closed A, so that paragraph supplies a proposed route under added data rather than an answer to the earlier unspecified case. No status in RESULTS_STATE is changed by this observation.', ['faisceau','local','compact'])
add('N33','024, e_n','unproved claim','Alors tous les F_A … satisfont e_n',f'{C147}, scans 181–184','adds a numerical dimension bound to the local stratification discussion','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The page defines an F-sheaf dimension bound through chains of rare closed sets and asserts its inheritance for closed A. The crossed-out “locᵗ” should be retained in the history of the claim: the live sentence restricts A to closed subsets. A comparison with o-minimal dimension must use the actual chain invariant and the chosen map from definable families, as set out in the answer to Q3.', ['dimension','fermé','fini'])
add('N34','024, analytic-torus example','unproved claim / counterexample offered','germes de parties analytiques d’un tore analytique de dim2',f'{C147}, scans182–183 (local structures and associated sheaf)','adds an obstruction to generating the local structure from global sections','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The example is offered to support strictness of the inclusion from the sheaf generated by Γ(X,underline F) into underline F. The page gives no construction of the torus or proof identifying all global sections, and its hypothesis is stated only as absence of nonconstant meromorphic functions. An audit should determine the precise permitted Boolean/local analytic family before using this as a proved example of that inclusion.', ['analytique','faisceau','locale'])
add('N35','024, final line','self-flagged / unfinished condition','f)',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (connected-stratum and germ conditions)','adds evidence that the sheaf version of the final axiom was left unwritten here','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The page announces a new condition and leaves only the label f). The later conditions in147 provide material for comparison, but filling this blank with them would change the source. The notes therefore record an unfinished definition rather than supply a guessed continuation.', ['connexes','stratification','faisceau'])
add('N36','026, mobility definitions','unproved claim','on peut alors choisir Y avec dim Y=ν',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (local product charts)','adds the dimension of the manifold direction as an invariant of a local product','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The definition exhibits the pair map (U,Y∩U)≅(N×Y_U,{a}×Y_U), and the NB asserts selection of an exactly ν-dimensional manifold direction. The last paragraph also asserts existence of a finite maximal mobility order under local finite dimensionality. Both assertions are stated without a separate dimensional proof, so the intended notion of dimension and the local chart restrictions remain part of the verification.', ['produit','dimension','local'])
add('N37','027, mobility loci','unproved claim','est un ouvert Mob^i(X)',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (local products)','adds an intrinsic filtration proposed before the stratified apparatus','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The open loci of i-mobile points and their closed complements are asserted before the questions labelled A–C. The inserted equivalence between exhaustion by F_i and existence of ν(x) is part of this setup, while the written F_3/F_2 ambiguity does not define a new filtration convention. A proof audit should transport the actual product charts to nearby points and establish the stated openness.', ['local','produit','filtration'])
add('N38','027, PropositionA','conjecture / self-flagged','on se pose la question … de la validité',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (local product condition imposed on strata)','adds a question about deriving strata intrinsically rather than taking them as given','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG H4 [unchecked hunch]',r'The page asks whether the exact mobility-i locus Y_i is a pure i-dimensional manifold along which X is equisingular. Its margin introduces “dévissables” for spaces satisfying this property, so the label PropositionA is not an unconditional proof. The later local-stratification definition in147 assumes a product structure; it does not by itself settle this intrinsic-existence question.', ['stratification','produit','variétés'])
add('N39','027, PropositionB and margin','conjecture / self-flagged','N est dévissable?',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 and190 (local normal models)','adds the immobile transverse factor and its proposed inheritance property','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'PropositionB asks for a local pair decomposition with an immobile transverse point and asserts constancy of its local homeomorphism type along a connected component. The margin separately asks that the normal factor N be dévissable. These are distinct tasks within the displayed product map, and the literal a/N wording is left marked in the transcription.', ['produit','fibration','local'])
add('N40','027, PropositionC','conjecture / self-flagged','le plus gros germe de sous-variété',f'{C147}, scans 181–183 (germs and local strata)','adds maximality and classification of equisingular manifold germs','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The question asks for Y_i to be the largest manifold germ carrying equisingularity and for all other such germs to correspond bijectively to regularly immersed submanifold germs of Y_i. The page supplies no map proving this claimed bijection beyond its inserted1–1 arrow. Its y/x ambiguity is a separate reading issue and should not be used to remove the maximality problem.', ['germe','strates','local'])
add('N41','028, PropositionD and diagram','conjecture / unproved claim','Y_ν(Y×N)=Y×Y_{ν−i}(N)',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,190 (product neighbourhoods)','adds a product-cancellation assertion for mobility','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG H4 [unchecked hunch]',r'The statement equates mobility in a product with shifted mobility of its transverse factor, and the margin uses it to link dévissability of N and Y×N to PropositionB. No proof is supplied, and the final qualification is explicitly uncertain between sous/sans réserve de PropA. Verification of the reverse direction requires recovering a transverse manifold direction from a product chart; that is substantive work beyond adding an evident factor.', ['produit','fibration','local'])
add('N42','030, change of ambient category','unpursued implication','objets et morphismes du contexte choisi',f'{C147}, scans140–146 (analytic, differentiable and topos contexts)','restates a dependence on the chosen category and allowed chart maps','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; MPL_150_001-043 Q4b [first-pass lead]',r'The local pair maps and the diagram maps are expressly required to be objects and morphisms in the chosen topological or piecewise category. Thus a comparison must retain the maps X′≅Y′×Z and the open embeddings Z_j×Y′→X_j, including their compatibility over i_0. The same source-level care is needed in147, where the author changes the category of neighbourhood constructions and marks resulting difficulties.', ['analytique','diff','topologique'])
add('N43','031, frontier proposition','unproved claim','l’adhérence de toute feuille est une réunion de feuilles',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (frontier and product conditions)','restates a frontier property, here asserted as a consequence of equisingularity','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The closure-of-a-leaf assertion is labelled Proposition but has no proof on the page. The route indicated by the definitions is to transport the incidence of a leaf through compatible local product charts along another leaf. The context later lists the frontier property as an axiom, so it provides a related formulation rather than a proof of this implication.', ['adhérence','produit','strates'])
add('N44','031–032, finiteness and closure leaves','unproved claim','une réunion finie de feuilles; corr. biunivoque',f'{C147}, scans 181,184 (local finiteness and compactness)','adds claims about finite closure decompositions and recovery of leaves from closures','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The page invokes compactness and local connectedness of filtration levels for the finite-union assertion, then claims F↦closure F is a bijection onto closed leaves. The written hypotheses must be checked for control of the number of filtration levels and of the components meeting a closure. The context’s explicit local-finiteness axiom identifies relevant additional data but does not retroactively insert it into031.', ['compact','fini','adhérence'])
add('N45','032, characterization by closed leaves','unproved claim','il f. et s.',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (product condition along closures)','restates the compatible local-product requirement in terms of the closed-leaf diagram','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The proposition characterizes equisingular filtrations by the frontier condition and simultaneous equisingularity of the diagram of all closed leaves. The definition immediately below then installs this diagrammatic requirement for a partition. The required comparison is between the filtration diagram and that closed-leaf diagram, including all inclusions; a collection of unrelated charts for individual leaves does not provide the displayed simultaneous data.', ['diagramme','produit','stratification'])
add('N46','033, four filtrations','unpursued implication','au moins4 façons canoniques',f'{C147}, scans185–188 (flags of incident strata)','adds several indexings of the same partition','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The manuscript explicitly notes that different filtrations can give the same leaves and lists dimension, incidence depth and their two dual constructions. These maps from a leaf-poset to filtration indices retain different numerical labels while the leaf partition is the common object. The subsequent flag construction in147 can be compared using the incidence poset itself, avoiding an unsupported identification of the four indexings.', ['drapeau','incidence','dimension'])
add('N47','033, inserted restriction proposition','unproved claim','parties loc. fermées … réunions de feuilles',f'{C147}, scans182,184 (open restriction)','adds restriction to locally closed saturated subsets','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The inserted proposition asserts inheritance of equisingularity by locally closed unions of leaves. Its proof would restrict the same compatible product charts and closed-leaf inclusions to the specified saturated subset. This statement has a concrete restricted domain and should be carried with that domain into comparisons with the context’s open restrictions.', ['restriction','ouvert','strates'])
add('N48','033–034, diagrams of leaf posets','unproved claim / reading question','de façon évidente',f'{C147}, scans185–189 (flags and face maps)','adds the proposed functorial leaf-incidence diagram','STRATA C.1,C.5 [return claims]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'The manuscript sends a leaf to its containing image leaf and then sends its closure to the closure of that image leaf, producing Φ_i→Φ_j. Admissibility itema) on033 is literally self-referential, so the precise admissibility input is a reading/formulation question. The claim that these maps assemble into the required closed-leaf diagram still needs every composition and incidence relation checked, just as147 later checks flag composition explicitly.', ['morphismes','drapeau','catégorie'])
add('N49','034, Conjecture1','conjecture','une plus grossière que toutes les autres',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (given stratifications); MPL_147_138-190_notes.md, discussion of local stratifications','adds existence and leastness of a privileged partition in the selected piecewise contexts','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; MPL_150_001-043 Q4b [first-pass lead]',r'The conjecture includes both existence of a partition with manifold leaves and a least such partition for the stated equisingularity condition. The replacement of “équisingulière” by “privilégiée” is part of the conjecture’s formulation, and the piecewise context is stated immediately above it. Neither a generic triangulation theorem nor a result about equivalence of PL object types supplies that leastness statement without a specific comparison of the permitted partitions.', ['stratification','variétés','local'])
add('N50','035, prescribed data before Conjecture2','conjecture / expectation','on voudrait trouver simultanément',f'{C147}, scans153–155 (admissible closed subsets and gluing)','adds compatibility with finitely many marked closed subsets and a specified map','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The requested partition must refine given admissible data, retain specified closed subsets as leaf unions, and work simultaneously with a map X→Y. These marked data are then essential in the recursive discussion on037. The conjectural coverage by the following finite-diagram statement should be verified by an actual encoding of those inclusions and that map in the finite diagram.', ['admissible','fermée','diagramme'])
add('N51','035, Conjecture2','conjecture','applications … propres; une moins fine',f'{C147}, scans153–155,185–189 (admissible subsets and diagram structure)','adds a canonical simultaneous partition for a finite proper diagram','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; BISITE D.6,D.11 and RESIDUE H.1 [return claims]',r'The statement explicitly assumes a finite ordered indexing set and proper maps and asks for a least privileged system. The context register’s direct-image comparisons concern specified constructible/categorical maps and do not establish this existence-and-leastness assertion. These pages contribute the geometric conjecture and the following attempted construction; they do not change the register status of those comparison results.', ['diagramme','morphismes','admissible'])
add('N52','035–036, image of a leaf','unproved claim (argument written across both scans)','l’image est Φ tout entier',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (local product models); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, BISITE D.5–D.7','adds a properness/local-product argument for surjectivity onto an image leaf','BISITE D.6 [Known, return claim]; RESIDUE G.5 [Proved, return claim]',r'The proof combines closedness from properness with openness from equisingularity and connectedness of the target leaf. Although the opening line says only “partition admissible,” the continuation actually invokes equisingularity, so that invoked input must be recorded in any reconstruction of the proof. This is a specific argument about f(F)⊆Φ; the register’s base-change statements require their own coefficient maps.', ['produit','fibré','connexe'])
add('N53','036, fibre-manifold assertion','unproved claim','les fibres … doivent aussi être des variétés',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,190 (local product/fibration claims)','adds a manifold-factor inference requiring the ambient-category restriction to be checked','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; RESIDUE G.5 [return claim]',r'The sentence infers that the fibre is a manifold from the local product map between manifold total and base leaves. The surrounding030–034 choice of piecewise morphisms matters to this step; the page gives no separate argument establishing the necessary factor property in that category. The concrete unrestricted-topological test in N54 isolates the issue without changing the conjecture’s stated category.', ['fibration','variétés','produit'])
add('N54','028 and036, product/fibre audit','own idea — explicit literature-based diagnostic','doivent aussi être des variétés',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,190; primary source [Bing58], p82','adds a specified map testing the unrestricted topological inference, without classifying the piecewise case','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]',r'Bing’s nonmanifold B has a homeomorphism h:B×R→R⁴; the composite p=pr_R∘h^{-1}:R⁴→R is a globally trivial bundle with fibre B. This gives an explicit failure of the inference from manifold total and base spaces to a manifold fibre in unrestricted topology, through that actual projection map [Bing58,Bing59]. Our diagnostic has high confidence from the cited construction; membership of p in the selected piecewise category and the mobility values required to test 028 are separate tasks left unclaimed here.', ['produit','fibration','variétés'])
add('N55','036, canonical partition of a proper map','conjecture','description conjecturale',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 (local product condition)','adds a proposed recursion for constructing the desired stratification of a map','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The recursion begins with the largest regular open U of the base over which X|U→U is locally trivial, and uses canonical partitions of fibres over that U. The paragraph attributes the intrinsic immobile-point construction to the first letter to A-Campo, a source pointer whose exact letter identification needs separate verification. The recursion is explicitly conjectural, so no existence theorem is supplied merely by naming U.', ['local','fibration','stratification'])
add('N56','036, required dimension drop','self-flagged','Il faut prouver que Y−U=Y′ … rare',f'{C147}, scans 181–182 and190 (local products still to be used)','adds a precise missing step in the canonical-map recursion','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]',r'The missing step has two parts: Y′ must remain an object of the selected category, and it must be rare with the stated lower dimension. A generic local-triviality assertion alone does not check closure in that category or the proposed maximality of U. The manuscript identifies this gap itself and does not close it before the package ends.', ['dimension','local','fibration'])
add('N57','037, closure stability','self-flagged','Il faut donc prouver que les overline F_i … sont encore des “espaces”',f'{C147}, scans 181–182,185 (closures and flags)','adds a second precise missing step in the recursion','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The marginal requirement is stability of the selected category under closures of the leaves constructed over U. Those closures are then restricted to Y′ to become new marked closed data in the recursive problem. The body writes Φ′_i while the margin writes overline F′_i; the frozen difference remains a reading question, without affecting the fact that the closure-stability obligation is explicit.', ['adhérence','fermé','strates'])
add('N58','037, strengthened induction','conjecture / self-flagged','il aurait fallu partir … une famille finie',f'{C147}, scans153–155 (admissible closed subsets)','adds a correction to the inductive input and a postponed construction','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]',r'The author recognizes that induction on a bare map is insufficient for his proposed construction and enlarges the input to a map with finitely many marked closed subspaces and their intersections. He then says the required intrinsic construction is “probablement” obtained by paraphrasing the first A-Campo letter. This is a stated method still to be completed, with the strengthened input and the unverified category-closure steps recorded separately.', ['admissible','fermée','intersection'])
add('N59','039, gluing triple','unpursued implication','(F,G,α); p*F→i*G',f'{C147}, scans156–172 (elementary pieces and amalgamations); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.6','adds an explicit coefficient-level gluing datum','STRATA C.6 [Proved, return claim]; BISITE F.9 [Known, return claim]',r'The drawn datum α:p*F→i*G is sent by the adjunction p*⊣p_* to F→p_*i*G via the unit followed by p_*α; the inverse sends β to the counit composed with p*β. These two operations are inverse by the adjunction identities and give the precise comparison with the triple-form gluing datum in STRATA C.6. The manuscript has not specified a higher coefficient enhancement here, so the comparison records this adjunction and does not silently change its coefficient category.', ['recollement','topos','faisceaux'])
add('N60','039, functor list and unfinished q!','unproved claim / unfinished calculation','q^!(G)=',f'{C147}, scans156–172; STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.6 and BISITE D.8','adds specific functor formulas and one empty right-hand side','BISITE F.9 [Known, return claim]; STRATA C.6 [Proved, return claim]',r'The page writes i′_*, i′*, p′_*, p′* and q_!, then leaves q^! without a right-hand side. The zero entries in the displayed triples and the dualizing-complex line signal coefficient choices that must be specified before verifying the adjunctions. The unfinished formula is a research item, and the clear exceptional exclamation marks have not been replaced by primes.', ['faisceaux','topos','recollement'])
add('N61','039, X_{I,J} and four operations','unproved claim / unpursued implication','α_*, α*, α_!, α^!; complexe dualisant',f'{C147}, scans157–162 (canonical locally closed and tubular topoi); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, BISITE D.6–D.8','adds a four-operation agenda for the indexed pieces','BISITE F.9 [Known, return claim]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]',r'The lower half proposes indexed differences X_{I,J}=X_I−X_J, maps between them and the four operations, followed by K^bullet_{X,Λ}. The actual maps α_{I,J/I′,J′} and their variance are the data to compare with the context’s canonical topoi; the page does not provide the functorial or base-change proofs. Nothing here resolves the unrestricted raw-space localization problem recorded as BISITE D.12.', ['topos','morphismes','local'])
add('N62','041, boundary-fibration data','unproved claim','fibres des variétés à bord',f'{C147}, scans173–178 (normal-bundle quotients and construction pieces)','adds manifold-boundary data for a general finite incidence system','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; EXIT_ONE_TYPE P1a1 [Proved, return claim]',r'The page stipulates V_i^circle and boundary submanifolds ∂_jV_i^circle fibred over V_j^circle, with restrictions on empty boundaries at minimal or predecessor indices. This is extra geometric data beyond the finite incidence poset, and the maps ∂_jV_i^circle→V_j^circle are the concrete comparison objects. The context’s normal-crossing pieces supply a special family of fibre models; no equivalence of the two general constructions is proved on041.', ['fibré','normal','strates'])
add('N63','041 and047, iterated boundaries','unproved claim','∂(∂_j V_i^circle)',f'{C147}, scans173–178,185–190; STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.5','adds explicit horizontal/relative boundary pieces and longer flags','STRATA C.5 [Proved, return claim]; EXIT_ONE_TYPE P1a1 [Proved, return claim]',r'The formulas decompose an iterated boundary into pullbacks of boundaries below and a relative fibre-boundary part. The grids on047 display the resulting restrictions, projections and cartesian-square crosses for longer flags. Matching these with147 requires the actual face maps and their compositions, including the relative-boundary summand; the uncertain pr/rel superscript remains unresolved.', ['drapeau','fibré','morphismes'])
add('N64','041–042, drawings of shared faces','unpursued implication','∂_210; V_210',f'{C147}, scans170–172 (amalgamated diagrams); {C149}, scans133–134 (maquette and fibre data)','adds visible incidence and shared-boundary information to the gluing programme','EXIT_ONE_TYPE P4e and FLAGGED_149 ZD8 [Proved, return claims]; WG H4 [unchecked hunch]',r'The drawings repeatedly mark the junction V_210 between the V_21 and V_20 boundary pieces. They therefore provide specific shared-face data to carry into a gluing construction, not only names for the individual strata. The context register already records limitations of a bare maquette as return claims; these drawings add manuscript evidence for retaining boundary attachments, without proving a complete reconstruction theorem.', ['maquette','recollement','bord'])
add('N65','043, coefficient/groupoid sketches','reading question / unproved claim','1-spécial; gr-poïde; 2-espèces|2-spéciaux',f'{C147}, scans178–180 (groupoids and Remords); {C149}, scans133–135','adds a difficult low-confidence sketch relevant to the reconstruction question','EXIT_ONE_TYPE P1d1,P1b1 [Proved, return claims]',r'The lower diagrams mention groupoids, a torsor expression and admissible functors, but several crucial words and indices are uncertain or cancelled. The supplied context makes these worth studying for the same reconstruction problem, while providing no licence to turn this sketch into a verified categorical presentation. In particular the torsor reading and the “2-espèces/2-spéciaux” alternative remain frozen and cannot support a historical claim of resolution.', ['groupoïde','topos','reconstituer'])
add('N66','044, reconstruction in seven data','unproved claim','reconstruction; On construit',f'{C147}, scans170–172 (amalgamated construction); STATEMENTS_WITH_STATUS.md, STRATA C.3,C.6','adds a two-stage geometric quotient recipe with explicit boundary fibrations','STRATA C.3,C.6 [return claims]; WG H4 [unchecked hunch]',r'The recipe builds V=V^circle amalgamated over U′ with U, and then W=W^circle amalgamated over V′ with V. The actual maps collapse the specified boundary fibres onto the lower pieces, so comparison with the context must retain V′→V and U′→U, not just the three strata U,V−U,W−V. Existence, uniqueness and recovery of the original equisingular structure are not proved on this page.', ['somme amalgamée','recollement','fibré'])
add('N67','044, item6 and adjacent diagram','reading question','∂U =|≃ ∂V^{prime circle}',f'{C147}, scans170–172 (amalgamations); {C149}, scan134 (explicit boundary maps)','adds a literal notation discrepancy inside the reconstruction recipe','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; STRATA C.3 [return claim]',r'Item6 literally has ∂U without double primes, whereas the adjacent diagram and pushout subscript use ∂U′′. The neighbouring expressions supply a mathematical consistency question but do not change the already frozen line. A reconstruction proof must state the domains of this boundary identification rather than silently use a corrected display.', ['recollement','fibré','morphismes'])
add('N68','045–047, examples and higher grid','unpursued implication / reading question','V_{ijkℓ}; variétés à bord fibrées',f'{C147}, scans185–190 (flags, composition, deferred fibrations)','adds explicit multistage models and coherence data to compare','STRATA C.5 [Proved, return claim]; WG H4 [unchecked hunch]',r'The examples on045 and the two grids on047 make the compatibility problem visible through multiple restrictions and crossed squares. The faint046 heading and traces, the n_j/n_i dimension label on047, and the missing circles at two row ends remain uncertain or literally absent, so a claimed general formula must not be inferred by filling them in. These pages provide models for checking the face maps of147, with no written proof of their general coherence.', ['drapeau','fibration','composition'])
add('N69','041–047, normal-crossing comparison task','own idea — specified comparison task','∂_jV_i^circle→V_j^circle',f'{C147}, scans173–178; {C149}, scans129–136','adds an explicit geometric comparison task while retaining normal and arithmetic data','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; LM6 F.43 and EXIT_ONE_TYPE P1a1,P4e [return claims]',r'Use a coordinate normal-crossing chart and send each boundary-angle tuple to its branch point and its angles; the face restriction forgets exactly the angles of the branches removed from the chosen flag. Compare those maps with the actual projections in047 and with the product of punctured normal-line bundles in147 before passing to the arithmetic groups T^J of149. This is our proposed check, with medium confidence because the local maps are explicit but global branch permutations, line-bundle twisting and the author’s chosen boundary realization still need verification; it claims neither a global equivalence nor a new theorem.', ['normal','drapeau','T^J'])
# Save a concise per-item literal search audit. The context texts themselves are not bundled again.
ctxparts=[]
for f in CTX.glob('*transcription.tex'):
 parts=re.split(r'\\scanpage\{(\d+)\}',f.read_text())
 for i in range(1,len(parts),2):ctxparts.append((f.name,int(parts[i]),parts[i+1]))
audit=[]
for n in notes:
 hits=[]
 for fn,s,b in ctxparts:
  terms=[t for t in n['search_terms'] if re.search(re.escape(t),b,re.I)]
  if terms:hits.append({'file':fn,'scan':s,'terms':terms})
 audit.append({'note':n['id'],'terms':n['search_terms'],'hits':hits})
(R/'records/research/root_notes.json').write_text(json.dumps(notes,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
(R/'records/research/context_search_audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(audit,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
out=['## Page-by-page research register\n\nEach item is separate from the frozen transcription. Context transcriptions are the supplied first-pass readings; their certainty has not been upgraded here.\n']
for n in notes:
 out.append(f"### {n['id']} — cote121, scans {n['scans']}\n\n**Kind:** {n['kind']}. **Anchor:** “{n['anchor']}”.\n\n**Context:** {n['context']}. **Relationship:** {n['relation']}. **Register:** {n['register']}.\n\n{n['text']}\n")
(R/'records/research/root_notes.md').write_text('\n'.join(out))
print('Wrote',len(notes),'research items and per-item context searches')
